<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarfaroshi Ki Tamanna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Sarfaroshi Ki Tamanna&quot; (&quot;the desire for sacrifice&quot;) is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urdu">Urdu</a> patriotic poem written by Bismil Azimabadi as a dedication to the young freedom fighters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> movement. It was written in 1921, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jallianwala-bagh-massacre">Jallianwala Bagh massacre</a> and other atrocities by the British colonial rulers, and first published in the journal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a>, published from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. It is a ghazal of 11 couplets.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Sarfaroshi Ki Tamanna</b>&quot; (&quot;the desire for sacrifice&quot;) is an Urdu patriotic poem written by Bismil Azimabadi as a dedication to the young freedom fighters of the Indian independence movement.</blockquote><a href="/songs/sarfaroshi-ki-tamanna">Sarfaroshi Ki Tamanna</a></li></ul></section>
